【TOP LEFT】: {date / series / project}
【TOP RIGHT】: {3 short concept words}
【BOTTOM LEFT】: {material / feature details}
【BOTTOM RIGHT】: {brand / product / studio name}
【FORMAT】: 9:16 vertical

Create a premium campaign poster using vertical sliced typography.

Place 【MAIN WORD】 large at the center, occupying about 80–88% of the width. Keep it bold, clear and readable at thumbnail size.

Use the entire word as a photographic mask for one single continuous photograph showing 【SUBJECT】 performing 【ACTION】 with 【PRODUCT / MATERIAL】.

Build the composition around one recognizable person, one clear product or material, and one strong motion element such as mist, a moving train, molten glass, steam or rotation. The scene should feel genuinely in motion rather than posed.

Keep roughly the upper 50–55% of the letterforms intact. Extend selected lower strokes downward into 4–6 sections with varied lengths, using them for clothing, tools, materials, reflections, floor or environment.

The same photograph must continue naturally through every letter and slice. Body position, tools, products and motion should align correctly across the word.

Strict clipping rule: all people, hair, products, tools, materials, mist, motion blur, steam and other photographic elements must stay completely inside the typography. Nothing should cross into the outer negative space.

Use a clean 【BACKGROUND】 with generous negative space, 【PALETTE】 for the photography, and a subtle soft shadow behind the type.

Arrange supporting information:

Top left: 【TOP LEFT】
Top right: 【TOP RIGHT】
Bottom left: 【BOTTOM LEFT】
Bottom right: 【BOTTOM RIGHT】

Use small, precise modern sans-serif typography.

The final result should feel like a finished lifestyle, product or process campaign—not a template demo.

Avoid broken faces, hands or tools, duplicated subjects, different images inside each letter, excessive slices, barcode-like strips, elements outside the type mask, random placeholder text, heavy 3D effects, watermarks, numbering, Vol., No., sparkle symbols or four-point stars.

